<!-- Risks Section -->
<div class="mt-8">
    <h2 id="investment-risks" class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span>⚠️</span>
        <span>Risks of SIP &amp; SWP Investments</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="bg-amber-50/60 p-5 rounded-2xl border border-amber-200/80 shadow-flat">
        <ul class="space-y-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700">
            <li><strong class="text-amber-900 font-semibold">Market Risk:</strong> Returns depend on mutual fund NAV performance. Equity SIPs can fluctuate in the short term (1–3 years), but historically yield strong inflation-beating returns over 7–10+ year horizons in India.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-amber-900 font-semibold">Sequence-of-Returns Risk (SWP):</strong> Severe market drawdowns early in retirement can accelerate capital depletion if withdrawal rates are too aggressive. Stress-test your plan using our built-in simulator.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-amber-900 font-semibold">Inflation Risk:</strong> Fixed-income returns (6–7%) often struggle against real consumer inflation (5–6%). Equity allocations in early SWP phases help maintain real purchasing power.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-amber-900 font-semibold">No Guaranteed Returns:</strong> Mutual fund investments are market-linked and not guaranteed like bank FDs. Past performance is not indicative of future returns.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>

